From ec43cfadc5fe856852233a5d43f988fce96e90c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:04:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/58] firmware: qcom: supply SCM reset controller device for
 ACPI

SCM registers a reset controller without an OF node during ACPI probe.
The reset core falls back to rcdev->dev to resolve the firmware node;
leaving both absent causes a NULL access in __dev_fwnode.

Set scm->reset.dev to the owning SCM device before
devm_reset_controller_register(). This gives the reset core a valid
device on ACPI while retaining the existing OF node on DT. The change
fixes reset-controller ownership metadata; it does not alter reset IDs
or secure-call semantics.
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index aa5b7ce20149546121a5e78e430c6756f8a0a953..e439e2c1e785041e9ca5639e7e0e029f6a18d313 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2777,6 +2777,7 @@ static int qcom_scm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(scm->bus_clk))
 		return PTR_ERR(scm->bus_clk);
 
+	scm->reset.dev = &pdev->dev;
 	scm->reset.ops = &qcom_scm_pas_reset_ops;
 	scm->reset.nr_resets = 1;
 	scm->reset.of_node = pdev->dev.of_node;
